            ['id' => 1, 'slug' => '5-signs-heart-attack-women', 'title' => '5 subtle signs of a heart attack in women', 'excerpt' => 'Heart disease presents differently in women. Here are the warning signs to know.', 'content' => "Heart disease is the leading cause of death for women worldwide, yet symptoms are often dismissed or misattributed.\n\nMany women experience warning signs weeks before a heart attack. Recognizing these early signals can save lives.\n\n## 1. Unexplained fatigue\n\nUnusual, persistent fatigue that interferes with daily activities is one of the most commonly reported pre-heart-attack symptoms in women.\n\n## 2. Shortness of breath\n\nIf climbing stairs or walking short distances leaves you winded when it didn't before, take note. This can occur without chest discomfort.\n\n## 3. Indigestion or nausea\n\nMany women mistake heart attack symptoms for acid reflux or the flu. Pressure or pain in the upper abdomen is a red flag.\n\n## 4. Jaw or neck pain\n\nRather than classic chest pain, women often report discomfort in the jaw, neck, or upper back that comes and goes.\n\n## 5. Cold sweat or dizziness\n\nBreaking out in a cold sweat or feeling lightheaded without a clear cause warrants immediate medical attention.\n\nIf you experience any combination of these symptoms, call emergency services right away.", 'category' => 'Cardiology', 'author' => 'Dr. Sarah Chen', 'author_id' => 1, 'published_at' => '2026-05-14 00:00:00', 'read_minutes' => 6, 'image' => 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559757175-5700dde675bc?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80', 'tags' => json_encode(['Heart Health', "Women's Health"])],
