            ['id' => 3, 'slug' => 'robotic-surgery-explained', 'title' => 'Robotic surgery, explained simply', 'excerpt' => 'What the surgeon controls, what the robot does, and what it means for recovery.', 'content' => "Robot-assisted surgery is one of the most misunderstood advancements in modern medicine.\n\nDespite the name, the surgeon is always in complete control. The robot is an extension of the surgeon's hands — a sophisticated tool that enhances precision.\n\n## How it works\n\nThe surgeon sits at a console and controls robotic arms that hold surgical instruments. A high-definition 3D camera provides magnified, immersive views of the operating site.\n\n## Benefits for patients\n\n- Smaller incisions — often just 1–2 cm\n- Less blood loss\n- Reduced pain and scarring\n- Shorter hospital stays\n- Faster return to normal activities\n\n## Is it right for you?\n\nRobotic surgery is ideal for many procedures including prostate surgery, hysterectomy, heart valve repair, and bariatric surgery.\n\nTalk to your surgeon about whether robotic-assisted techniques are appropriate for your specific condition.", 'category' => 'Innovation', 'author' => 'Dr. Marcus Thorne', 'author_id' => 3, 'published_at' => '2026-06-10 00:00:00', 'read_minutes' => 8, 'image' => 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1631815589968-fdb09a223b1e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80', 'tags' => json_encode(['Surgery', 'Technology'])],
